{/*
  Site footer. RESTRUCTURED 2026-08-23 (Jon) to:

    1. MEDICAL DISCLAIMER at the TOP
    2. brand + ONE uniform all-caps menu of all six links, Contact last
    3. copyright on its own line beneath

  Previously three blocks - brand/links, then disclaimer, then a bottom bar with
  the legal links. That put two link groups doing the same job at opposite ends
  with the disclaimer wedged between them. Jon: "combine the two sections of
  links... make the whole menu caps... Contact last item in nav."

  Podcast link REMOVED 2026-08-21 (Jon). Not pursuing podcasting: "people wont
  listen. those podcasts are basically long testimonials for my services." Any
  interviews go on the YouTube channel. /podcast was never built and was 404ing
  from every page. Do not re-add it.

  Also gone, and not to be restored: the "Always be quitting… until you've quit
  for the last time" tagline (it repeated the final CTA section), and the "Work
  With Jon" gold heading (it labelled a vertical stack that no longer exists).
*/}
<footer class="footer">
  {/* Disclaimer first (Jon, 2026-08-23). Centred, capped at 78ch - genuinely
      full width would give ~180-character lines. */}
  <section class="footer__legal" aria-label="Medical disclaimer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="footer__legal-heading">Medical Disclaimer</p>
      <p class="footer__legal-body">
        The content, programs, and services offered by ABQ are for education only. This is not medical or
        mental health treatment. You assume all risks if you choose to apply it to yourself or others.
        Consult with your health care provider regarding the appropriateness of it to your situation.
        See our <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> for complete details.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ONE menu (Jon, 2026-08-23): all six links, uniformly styled, all caps,
      Contact last. Previously two navs - offers and legal - styled differently
      at opposite ends. They are now a single nav semantically as well as
      visually, which is the honest markup: two aria-labelled groups made sense
      when they looked like two groups.

      Copyright sits on its own line below. Six uppercase links plus the brand
      plus a copyright line will not fit on one row at any realistic width. */}
  <div class="footer__bottom">
    <div class="wrap footer__bar">
      <p class="footer__logo">ALWAYS BE QUITTING</p>
      <nav class="footer__menu" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="/community">The ABQ Community</a>
        <a href="/coaching">1:1 Coaching</a>
        <a href="/free-guide">Free Quick-Start Guide</a>
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    {/* Location removed 2026-08-23 (Jon): "i am not competing locally."
         The Blacksburg reference in /terms is the arbitration venue and is
         legally load-bearing - do not remove that one. */}
    <p class="wrap footer__copy">© 2026 Motivation and Mindset Studios, LLC</p>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .footer {
    background: var(--teal-deep);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 80%, var(--teal-deep));
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* ---- 1. medical disclaimer, now the TOP block ---- */
  .footer__legal {
    padding-block: 2rem;
  }
  /* Centred and capped: left-aligned at 70ch it filled half the width and left
     the right side empty; genuinely full width would give ~180-char lines. */
  .footer__legal-heading {
    font: 800 0.72rem/1 var(--font-body);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .footer__legal-body {
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block: 0;
    max-width: 78ch;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 68%, var(--teal-deep));
  }
  .footer__legal-body a {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 88%, var(--teal-deep));
  }

  /* ---- 2. brand + one uniform menu, copyright beneath ---- */
  .footer__bottom {
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 16%, transparent);
    padding-block: 1.4rem;
  }
  .footer__bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.9rem 2rem;
  }
  /* Brand stays larger and white so it does not get lost among six uppercase
     links that now share its casing. */
  .footer__logo {
    font: 800 1rem/1 var(--font-body);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* One menu, uniform treatment. Offers and legal are no longer distinguished
     by styling - Jon wanted a single menu, so they read as one set. */
  .footer__menu {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.4rem;
  }
  .footer__menu a {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 72%, var(--teal-deep));
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .footer__menu a:hover {
    color: var(--white);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .footer__copy {
    margin: 1.1rem auto 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 55%, var(--teal-deep));
  }
</style>
